AWS Public VPC and EC2 Infrastructure Setup
This repository contains documentation and deployment scripts for configuring a public-facing Virtual Private Cloud (VPC) architecture on Amazon Web Services (AWS) in the us-east-1 region, adhering to requirements specified by the Nautilus DevOps Team.

Architecture Overview
VPC: devops-pub-vpc (10.0.0.0/16) with DNS support and DNS hostnames enabled.

Internet Gateway: devops-pub-igw attached to the VPC to enable outbound and inbound internet connectivity.

Route Table: devops-pub-rt featuring a default route (0.0.0.0/0) targeting the Internet Gateway.

Public Subnet: devops-pub-subnet (10.0.0.0/24) configured with auto-assignment of public IPv4 addresses enabled (MapPublicIpOnLaunch: true).

Security Group: devops-pub-sg allowing inbound SSH access (TCP port 22) from any IP address (0.0.0.0/0).

EC2 Instance: devops-pub-ec2 (t2.micro) running in the public subnet with an allocated public IP address.

Deployment & Configuration via AWS CLI
1. Create and Configure the VPC
Bash
VPC_ID=$(aws ec2 create-vpc --cidr-block 10.0.0.0/16 --region us-east-1 --tag-specifications 'ResourceType=vpc,Tags=[{Key=Name,Value=devops-pub-vpc}]' --query 'Vpc.VpcId' --output text)

aws ec2 modify-vpc-attribute --vpc-id $VPC_ID --enable-dns-hostnames
aws ec2 modify-vpc-attribute --vpc-id $VPC_ID --enable-dns-support
2. Set Up Internet Gateway and Route Table
Bash
IGW_ID=$(aws ec2 create-internet-gateway --region us-east-1 --tag-specifications 'ResourceType=internet-gateway,Tags=[{Key=Name,Value=devops-pub-igw}]' --query 'InternetGateway.InternetGatewayId' --output text)
aws ec2 attach-internet-gateway --internet-gateway-id $IGW_ID --vpc-id $VPC_ID

RT_ID=$(aws ec2 create-route-table --vpc-id $VPC_ID --region us-east-1 --tag-specifications 'ResourceType=route-table,Tags=[{Key=Name,Value=devops-pub-rt}]' --query 'RouteTable.RouteTableId' --output text)
aws ec2 create-route --route-table-id $RT_ID --destination-cidr-block 0.0.0.0/0 --gateway-id $IGW_ID --region us-east-1
3. Create the Public Subnet
Bash
SUBNET_ID=$(aws ec2 create-subnet --vpc-id $VPC_ID --cidr-block 10.0.0.0/24 --availability-zone us-east-1a --region us-east-1 --tag-specifications 'ResourceType=subnet,Tags=[{Key=Name,Value=devops-pub-subnet}]' --query 'Subnet.SubnetId' --output text)

aws ec2 modify-subnet-attribute --subnet-id $SUBNET_ID --map-public-ip-on-launch
aws ec2 associate-route-table --subnet-id $SUBNET_ID --route-table-id $RT_ID --region us-east-1
4. Configure Security Group and Ingress Rules
Bash
SG_ID=$(aws ec2 create-security-group --group-name devops-pub-sg --description "Allow SSH access" --vpc-id $VPC_ID --region us-east-1 --query 'GroupId' --output text)

aws ec2 authorize-security-group-ingress --group-id $SG_ID --protocol tcp --port 22 --cidr 0.0.0.0/0 --region us-east-1
5. Launch the EC2 Instance
Bash
AMI_ID=$(aws ec2 describe-images --owners amazon --filters "Name=name,Values=amzn2-ami-hvm-*-x86_64-gp2" --query 'sort_by(Images, &CreationDate)[-1].ImageId' --output text --region us-east-1)

aws ec2 run-instances \
    --image-id $AMI_ID \
    --instance-type t2.micro \
    --subnet-id $SUBNET_ID \
    --security-group-ids $SG_ID \
    --associate-public-ip-address \
    --region us-east-1 \
    --tag-specifications 'ResourceType=instance,Tags=[{Key=Name,Value=devops-pub-ec2}]'
Verification
To verify that the infrastructure is up and running correctly, execute:

Bash
aws ec2 describe-instances --filters "Name=tag:Name,Values=devops-pub-ec2" --region us-east-1 --query "Reservations[*].Instances[*].{ID:InstanceId,State:State.Name,PublicIP:PublicIpAddress}"
